<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Our project solves this by creating one framework that can train and run a variety of models, all using the same command structure. Whether you want to fine-tune GPT-2 on a custom dataset, generate images with CGAN or CVAE, or synthesize audio with WaveGAN, you can do it with a single, consistent command. The framework is modular, so adding new models or datasets is straightforward, and it automatically handles dataset preparation, logging, and result storage. This makes it not just a learning project, but a practical tool for anyone working with generative AI.)
/E (Our project solves this by creating one framework that can train and run a variety of models, all using the same command structure. Whether you want to fine-tune GPT-2 on a custom dataset, generate images with CGAN or CVAE, or synthesize audio with WaveGAN, you can do it with a single, consistent command. The framework is modular, so adding new models or datasets is straightforward, and it automatically handles dataset preparation, logging, and result storage. This makes it not just a learning project, but a practical tool for anyone working with generative AI.)
/Pg 8 0 R
>>
